A small linear video editor using a QT6 interface capable of copy (lossless)
and encoding modes. In copy mode, it can cut and rejoin (splice) streams 
between keyframes (I-frames) and remux the result without re-encoding. By 
appending the same video, you can reorder or repeat keyframe segments as 
desired while in copy mode. In encoding mode, Avidemux can apply filters 
(resizing, cropping, masking, deinterlacing, colour manipulation, OpenGL, 
etc.) and re-encode to a choice of codecs (H.264, H.265, AV1, VP9, etc.) 
and containers (MP4, MKV, TS, etc.).
